Chapter: FsReadTextScope
  cites Foreword chapter FileSystem

 read-text is the handler-dispatched read of the FileSystem layer, and a
 handler must not be a way around a scope. This opening grants itself
 FileSystem.Read under "/config/" and then asks read-text for
 /etc/passwd. The scope check keys on the operation's name before any
 handler is consulted, so the refusal lands at compile time exactly as
 it does for the builtin-backed file-exists -- if this ever compiles,
 scoping an effect the layer serves means nothing.

Section: Body
  opening : [Console, FileSystem.Read "/config/"] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (read-text "/etc/passwd")
  end
